warren buffett is generally regarded as  the best investor of all time which is  not surprising given his insane track  history he has managed to achieve an  average annual return of 20.5 since 1965  and while buffett does deserve all the  praise he receives someone that often  doesn't get enough credit is charlie  munger charlie is the vice chairman of  berkshire hathaway and has known buffett  since 1959. buffett says that he knew  that he wasn't going to find another guy  like monger as soon as he met him so  hiring monger was a no-brainer for  buffett since then monger has become  buffett's closest ally and business  partner and together dave shaped  berkshire into what it is today  charlie is now a multi-billionaire  himself thanks to the phenomenal  performance of berkshire hathaway yet  most people have no idea who monger even  is especially in comparison to buffett  so here's how monger became the silent  backbone of berkshire hathaway  taking a look back charles thomas monger  was born on january 1 1924 in omaha  nebraska monger had a pretty nice  childhood as he came from a pretty wild  family monger's grandfather himself was  a district court judge and a state  representative meanwhile monger's father  was a lawyer considering this background  i don't think you'd be surprised here  that monger would eventually end up  pursuing a law degree but as a teenager  monger would find himself working at a  local grocery store named buffett and  son as you would guess this door was  owned by buffett's grandfather and this  was monger's first introduction to the  family monger would go on to attend the  university of michigan where he matured  in mathematics but just as he enrolled  pearl harbor would be bombed resulting  in manga dropping out of college and  enlisting in the u.s army corps which  would eventually become the air force  while this was quite a turn of events it  wasn't all bad for monger he would soon  be stationed in alaska where he met a  woman named nancy hoggins who would soon  become his wife apart from this however  wenger found little joy in the air force  he was nominated by all the death and  destruction that he saw on a daily basis  one of the few things that kept him sane  during this time period was playing  cards with his colleagues and this is  where he learned many of the principles  that he would later apply to investing  monger says that cards taught him to  fold early when the odds are against him  and doubled down when he had the edge  playing cards also taught him that  opportunity does not come often which  makes it especially important to seize  opportunity when it does come anyway the  war would finally come to an end in 1945  and monger would leave the military  shortly after by this point wanker  didn't want to go back and finish his  bachelor's but he did want to pursue a  law degree  fortunately the gi bill would help  monger do exactly this he went ahead and  took a bunch of advanced courses at  caltech and he would leverage this  experience to sneak his way into harvard  law school without a bachelor's despite  not having a bachelor's law school was a  breeze from mongura as he would end up  graduating magna [ __ ] laude in 1948 and  with that monger was officially a lawyer  after graduation monger and his new  family would move to california where he  found a job at a law firm called wright  and garrett for most people this would  be the pinnacle of life as monger had  secured a solid job and family but it  wouldn't take long for everything to  unravel  after eight years of marriage and three  children mongre and nancy would decide  to split ways which was not only  challenging emotionally but also  financially monger would end up losing  most of his money and his house to the  divorce and the monger would end up  spending the next few years simply  working back to where he was to make  things worse divorce was heavily  stigmatized at the time which did not  earn monger much respect from his peers  and just when you think that things  can't get worse they got way worse  monger's son teddy would be diagnosed  with leukemia monger didn't have health  insurance so he not only had to pay for  all of the treatment out of pocket but  he had to slowly watch his son get  weaker and weaker for 11 months before  passing away at age 9. around the same  time monger's father would also pass  away which forced monger to return home  and support his family for some time the  one good thing that came out of this  visit was that he would end up meeting a  man named warren buffett the two would  quickly become friends and exchange  contact info but both of them would  return to their own lives after the  visit was over after returning to  california monger would eventually  develop cataracts which forced him to  get surgery in his left eye  unfortunately the surgery would go wrong  which left him blind in his left eye he  held onto the blind eye for some time  but he eventually got his surgically  removed due to severe pain to make  things worse doctors told him that blood  would eventually fill up his right eye  as well which would make him completely  blind so monger would actually begin  learning braille but thankfully monger  would finally catch a break and the  condition would slowly recede clearly  monger had quite a difficult life  throughout his 30s and 40s but here's  what monger had to say about it you do  not want to drift into self-pity  self-pity will not improve the situation  before returning to nebraska for his  father's death bunker would actually  find a second wife ironically her name  was also nancy but this marriage would  end up working far better than the first  despite it being unorthodox for the time  both monger and nancy had two children  each from their previous marriages and  together they would form a new family of  six  these two would end up staying together  for the next 54 years until nancy passed  away in 2010 anyway after his father's  death monger decided to start fresh by  launching his own business in 1962. this  new business was called mongur tools and  olsen and it provided real estate  attorney services while his day job was  still being a lawyer manga spent most of  his free time meddling with the stock  market he had his ups and downs and the  income wasn't super consistent but  monger saw opportunity in the stock  market and he didn't waste time seizing  it soon enough he left law altogether  and partnered with jack wheeler to  launch an investment firm called the  wheeler monger and company at first  monger saw a significant amount of  success  for years he was averaging 20 annual  returns which was four times higher than  the market at the time but the 1970s  would bring with it a lot of pain not  just for monger but for all investors in  general in 1971 president nixon would  drop the gold standard which sent  inflation to the moon and stocks to rock  bottom the s p 500 would face multiple  bear markets throughout this decade and  stocks would basically make no progress  monger was by no means immune to this  market downturn and his investments  would get crushed in 1973 monger would  lose 32 percent and in 1974 he would  lose another 31 percent fortunately the  stock market had a massive rebound in  1975 which allowed monger to post a 73.2  return monger took this as a signal that  he should leave while he still could and  he would close up wheeler manga and  company in 1976 and that marks the end  of monger's days of running his own  business a few years later in 1978  monger would join buffett's company as  vice chairman and the rest is history  while monger technically always worked  under buffett on paper buffett never  treated him as an employee rather  buffett always treated monger as a  business partner in 1984 monger was made  the ceo and chairman of west coast  financial which was a company that  berkshire hathaway had a majority stake  in and this is where monger 